course: dictionary
lesson: 4583
title: Helpless and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Helpless means not able to look after yourself or do things without help. A newborn baby is helpless: it needs a grown-up to feed it and keep it safe. «Some babies, like kittens, puppies and human babies, are born helpless and need long care.» The words «need long care» are the clue.
explain: Helpless can also mean unable to change a bad situation or stop something happening. «Seeing a parent collapse is very scary; knowing how to call the emergency number and what to say helps children feel less helpless.» The clue is that knowing what to do makes you feel less powerless. So helpless means you feel you cannot do anything.
explain: Read the words around the word. «The old gaoler's rusty key creaks, the door clangs, and Toad is a helpless prisoner.» A prisoner is locked in, so helpless means unable to help himself or get free. Try your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense? Yes.
fact: Helpless means not able to look after yourself or do things without help.
fact: A newborn baby, a kitten or a puppy can be helpless.
fact: Helpless can also mean unable to stop a bad thing from happening.
fact: «Helpless» is not the same as weak: «Plant-eaters were not helpless» because Stegosaurus, Triceratops and Ankylosaurus had spikes, horns and armour to protect themselves.
fact: Helpless laughter is laughter you cannot stop.
exercise: «Some babies, like kittens and human babies, are born helpless.» What does helpless mean here? | *Not able to look after themselves without help | Very loud and noisy | Happy to be left alone | Able to look after themselves
exercise: «Plant-eaters were not helpless: Stegosaurus had tail spikes, Triceratops horns and a frill.» What does this tell you? | Plant-eaters could not eat | Plant-eaters had no way to protect themselves | Plant-eaters were always hungry | *Plant-eaters had ways to protect themselves
exercise: «Her laughter was helpless, and she could not stop giggling.» What does helpless laughter mean? | Laughter at a sad film | Laughter that is very quiet | *Laughter you cannot stop | Laughter that is rude
test: «Toad is a helpless prisoner.» What does helpless mean? | Hungry for food | Very kind and friendly | *Unable to help himself or get free | Able to escape easily
test: Mia says, «I feel helpless when I see someone in trouble.» What does she mean? | She is happy to watch | She wants to be in trouble | *She feels she cannot change the bad situation | She is very strong
exam: Which situation shows someone who is helpless to stop something bad? | *A child trapped in a locked room with no key and no way to call for help | A child eating a big lunch | A child reading a book about dinosaurs | A child who is playing happily in the park
